<https://w3id.org/ci> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/ci> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://w3id.org/cterm> .
<https://w3id.org/ci> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "L'ontologia Cost Item (CI) fornisce un modello semantico per rappresentare e strutturare le voci di costo delle costruzioni e le relative componenti. Distingue le opere fisiche dalle attività di costruzione e supporta la descrizione delle informazioni di costo mediante terminologia standardizzata, attributi quantitativi, unità di misura e informazioni economiche. CI è progettata per interoperare con le ontologie Construction Resources (CR) e Construction Terminology (CTERM)."@it .
<https://w3id.org/ci> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "The Cost Item (CI) Ontology provides a semantic model for representing and structuring construction cost items and their constituent components. It separates physical works from construction activities and supports the description of cost information through standardized terminology, quantitative attributes, units, and economic information. CI is designed to interoperate with the Construction Resources (CR) and Construction Terminology (CTERM) ontologies."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ci> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Cassandro, J., Hagedorn, P., Sigalov, K., Gatto, C., Mirarchi, C., Pavan, A., & König, M. (2025). Semantic Integration of Cost, Time and Geometry for a Resource-centred Perspective of Managing Construction Projects: . Proceedings of the 2025 European Conference on Computing in Construction. Publiziert. European Conference on Computing in Construction, Porto. https://doi.org/10.35490/ec3.2025.263" .
